(version 1)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MP6541A (TQFN-26 6x6mm, FCQFN) fine-pitch land pattern
#
# MPS's recommended land pattern places the centre power bars 0.100 mm from the
# side pads:
#
#     side pad   x = +/-2.50, half-width 0.40  ->  inner edge +/-2.10
#     centre bar x = +/-1.80, half-width 0.20  ->  outer edge +/-2.00
#                                                  gap = 0.100 mm
#
# That is tighter than the board's 0.2 mm Default netclass clearance, so DRC
# reports 16 pad-pairs per device (U14, U15) that are inherent to the part and
# cannot be fixed by moving anything.
#
# This rule relaxes clearance to 0.1 mm ONLY where both items belong to an
# MP6541A footprint, so the global 0.2 mm still applies to everything routed
# near the part.
#
# FAB CHECK: 0.10 mm (~4 mil) spacing exceeds JLCPCB's standard 0.127 mm
# process -- confirm your fabricator supports it before relying on this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(rule "MP6541A intra-footprint clearance"
    (condition "A.Library_Link == 'ProPrj_Dri-easyedapro:TQFN-26 (6X6MM)' && B.Library_Link == 'ProPrj_Dri-easyedapro:TQFN-26 (6X6MM)'")
    (constraint clearance (min 0.1mm))
)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# USB-C receptacle and tactile switches -- edge clearance reviewed & accepted
#
# USB1 is an edge-mounted Type-C receptacle: its pads and the VBUS traces
# feeding them necessarily sit close to the connector's own board cutout, and
# its SHELL through-holes sit close to the outer edge.  SW2/SW3 are likewise
# placed hard against the edge by design.
#
# Observed range for this set: 0.155 .. 0.462 mm against the 0.5 mm global
# rule.  0.15 mm covers it.
#
# Scope note: this deliberately does NOT cover the BEAMBREAK track, which runs
# 0.30-0.41 mm from the INTERNAL circular cutout on Inner1.  That one is a
# routing choice, not connector geometry, and should be moved rather than
# excused.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(rule "USB-C / switch edge clearance (reviewed, accepted)"
    (condition "A.Reference == 'USB1' || A.Reference == 'SW2' || A.Reference == 'SW3' || A.insideCourtyard('USB1')")
    (constraint edge_clearance (min 0.15mm))
)
